{"id":"C1-L047","title":"refrain from doing — form","cefr":"C1","level":"C1","unit":"C1-U03","focus":"refrain from doing — forma","targets":{"grammar":"refrain from doing — forma","pron":"Expressividade","verbs":[],"pv":[],"expr":[],"words":["research restraint","bold claim","selective citation","duplicate publication","code of conduct","unpublished draft","integrity policy","cautious language","overstated finding","trust over time","scientific honesty","hedging term","publication ethics","salami slicing","self-plagiarism","misleading headline","conflict declaration","reviewer duty","confidential manuscript","author guidelines","overclaiming","modest conclusion"],"field":"Pesquisa","genre":"Texto acadêmico e resumo","skill":"Fala","words_min":22},"frames":[{"tag":"Abertura","title":"Lesson 47 · refrain from doing — form","blocks":[{"type":"box","kind":"look","t":"Nesta aula","body":["**Foco:** refrain from doing — forma.","**Pronúncia:** Expressividade.","**22 palavras novas** (pesquisa).","**Texto do dia:** texto acadêmico e resumo."]},{"type":"p","t":"**Objetivo de comunicação (C1):** eu consigo usar refrain from doing (e verbos parecidos: abstain from, desist from, be prohibited from) num texto acadêmico sobre integridade científica."},{"type":"box","kind":"exam","t":"Ponte para as provas","body":["","Esta aula treina **responder em frases completas (IELTS Speaking, TOEFL Speaking)**."]}]},{"tag":"Aquecimento","title":"Warm-up · Say the words","blocks":[{"type":"p","t":"Toque em 🔊, ouça e repita cada palavra. Depois tente adivinhar o sentido."},{"type":"words","items":[["research restraint","cautela na pesquisa"],["bold claim","afirmação ousada"],["selective citation","citação seletiva"],["duplicate publication","publicação duplicada"],["code of conduct","código de conduta"],["unpublished draft","rascunho inédito"],["integrity policy","política de integridade"],["cautious language","linguagem cautelosa"],["overstated finding","achado exagerado"],["trust over time","confiança ao longo do tempo"],["scientific honesty","honestidade científica"],["hedging term","termo de atenuação"],["publication ethics","ética da publicação"],["salami slicing","fatiamento de publicações"],["self-plagiarism","autoplágio"],["misleading headline","manchete enganosa"],["conflict declaration","declaração de conflitos"],["reviewer duty","dever do avaliador"],["confidential manuscript","manuscrito confidencial"],["author guidelines","diretrizes para autores"],["overclaiming","exagero de conclusões"],["modest conclusion","conclusão modesta"]]}]},{"tag":"Leitura","title":"Reading · An academic text","blocks":[{"type":"text","title":"Abstract: Restraint in Scientific Reporting","paras":["Researchers are expected to **refrain from overstating** their findings. The code of conduct asks authors to **abstain from selective citation** and to **desist from republishing** the same data. Reviewers, in turn, are **prohibited from using** unpublished material.","The study shows that those who **refrain from making** bold claims are cited **less** at first, but trusted **more** later."],"kicker":"ABSTRACT","by":"Journal of Research Integrity","gloss":[["overstate","exagerar"],["selective","seletivo"],["code of conduct","código de conduta"],["bold","ousado"]]}]},{"tag":"Compreensão","title":"Did you understand?","blocks":[{"type":"tfng","title":"","items":[{"q":"Authors are expected to overstate findings.","ans":"F","why":"refrain from overstating."},{"q":"Reviewers may use unpublished material.","ans":"F","why":"prohibited from using."},{"q":"Cautious authors gain trust later.","ans":"T","why":"trusted more later."}]},{"type":"mcq","title":"Vocabulary in context","items":[{"q":"“refrain from” = ?","opts":["abster-se de","refrescar","repetir"],"ans":0,"why":"refrain from overstating."},{"q":"“overstate” = ?","opts":["exagerar","subestimar","declarar"],"ans":0,"why":"overstating."}]}]},{"tag":"Gramática","title":"refrain from + -ing","blocks":[{"type":"table","head"